{
  "description": "A diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that examines each trained NextItNet category model through the host ModelView interface. It reports measured metrics with definitions and constructs an interpretation prompt grounded in those measurements.",
  "motivation": "Make model diagnosis compatible with the actual sequential backbone while preventing unsupported conclusions about unavailable reviews, item attributes, or simulator traits. Model selection remains based on macro-average validation HR@10 across all four datasets.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Preserve view.model, item_emb, log2feats(sequence), predict_score(features, items), user_train, meta_data, and review_data interfaces. Consume batches shaped B x L containing (None, sequence, positive, negative), excluding padding from measurements. For left-padded histories, read the final nonpadding position rather than count-1. Use only observed histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; mark unsupported analyses unavailable. Preserve one independently trained NextItNet model/checkpoint per category and predictor consistency. No diagnostic results or performance gains are supplied in the description.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n  initialize(view, device)\n  run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n    save model training state\n    put view.model in evaluation mode\n    under no_grad:\n      for (_, sequence, positive, negative) in train_loader:\n        features = view.log2feats(sequence)\n        identify valid sequence and target positions\n        compute supported diagnostic measurements through ModelView\n        accumulate measurements and sample counts\n    restore model training state\n    return {metrics: aggregated measurements,\n            metric_definitions: definitions, populations, and limitations}\n\ndiagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n  construct prompt from measured metrics and their definitions\n  identify unavailable evidence explicitly\n  request NextItNet-compatible hypotheses respecting the single-model constraint",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Provides a task-specific interface connecting native diagnosis to NextItNet and the pinned benchmark.",
    "negative": "Primarily an integration specification; it introduces no new diagnostic estimator or learning algorithm."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support evidence-based architecture and training changes through consistent, reproducible diagnostics.",
    "negative": "Utility depends on probe design and validation; diagnostic correlations alone do not establish improvements in HR@10."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required entry points, batch format, and compatibility interfaces are explicit.",
    "negative": "Correct padding masks, feature alignment, measurement aggregation, and architecture-specific probes require care."
  }
}
